<HelpTab>
    <FluentText>
        Add the <strong>Operations Alerts</strong> widget to a dashboard to keep the open alerts in view. In the dashboard
        editor, add a widget and pick <strong>Operations Alerts</strong>.
    </FluentText>

    <HelpSection Title="What it shows">
        <ul>
            <li>The same open alerts as the Operations alerts page, for the locations you manage, most severe first.</li>
            <li>How many are still open, and a <strong>View all alerts</strong> link to the full page.</li>
            <li><strong>Acknowledge</strong> and <strong>Resolve…</strong> work from the widget too. New alerts appear
                without reloading.</li>
        </ul>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Settings">
        <FluentText>Right-click the widget while editing the dashboard:</FluentText>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Show</strong>: every alert, warnings and critical only, or critical only.</li>
            <li><strong>Hide alerts someone has acknowledged</strong>: only show the ones nobody has picked up yet.</li>
        </ul>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpNote>
        Each person sees the alerts for their own locations, so the same dashboard can show different alerts to an Admin and
        a Manager. A dashboard shown on a kiosk has nobody signed in, so the widget asks you to sign in instead.
    </HelpNote>
</HelpTab>
